---
import PageLayout from '../layouts/PageLayout.astro';
import ContentNote from '../components/content/ContentNote.astro';
import RelatedReading from '../components/content/RelatedReading.astro';
---

<PageLayout
  title="Advertising Policy | Cooked Finance"
  description="Cooked Finance does not currently carry ads. Read our standards for any future advertising, labelling, privacy, placement, and editorial independence."
  path="/advertising-policy"
  eyebrow="Commercial transparency"
  heading="No ads today. Clear rules before any arrive."
  lead="Cooked Finance has not applied for Google AdSense and does not currently display paid advertising."
  updated="August 17, 2026"
>
  <ContentNote title="Current status">
    <p>
      The site plans to consider an AdSense application only after it has a mature
      content library and a stable audience of roughly 100–200 visitors per day.
      That traffic target is our own publishing decision, not a stated AdSense
      eligibility rule. No application or approval is implied by this page.
    </p>
  </ContentNote>

  <h2>Rules for future advertising</h2>
  <p>If Cooked Finance introduces ads, the following standards will apply:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>Ads will be visually distinguishable from navigation, calculator controls, results, and editorial recommendations.</li>
    <li>Ad units will use clear labels such as “Advertisement” or “Sponsored links,” as applicable.</li>
    <li>Payment will not change Cooked Score formulas, score ranges, benchmark interpretation, editorial conclusions, or internal rankings.</li>
    <li>Ads will not be positioned to look like a required next step or a personalized recommendation.</li>
    <li>Advertising relationships will not buy positive coverage, hidden links, or removal of accurate criticism.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Places we do not plan to monetize with display ads</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>The calculator input flow</li>
    <li>Personalized score results and component explanations</li>
    <li>The methodology and source-policy pages</li>
    <li>Privacy, legal, corrections, and advertising-policy pages</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    If display advertising is introduced, initial placements should be limited to
    substantive guides and benchmark explainers after readers have received useful
    content. Any later change to this approach should be reflected here.
  </p>

  <h2>Financial-input privacy</h2>
  <p>
    Income, expenses, cash balances, debt payments, contribution amounts,
    retirement balances, Cooked Score, component scores, and result labels must
    not be sent to advertising platforms, used to build advertising audiences,
    placed in ad-request parameters, or exposed in shareable URLs. Advertising
    must not be personalized from the financial values entered into the calculator.
  </p>

  <h2>Consent and third parties</h2>
  <p>
    Before activating advertising technology, Cooked Finance will update its
    privacy disclosures, implement legally required consent controls, and publish
    the appropriate advertising-system records. Third-party vendors may have their
    own data practices, which will be linked from the privacy policy when relevant.
  </p>

  <h2>Sponsored and affiliate content</h2>
  <p>
    Cooked Finance does not currently publish sponsored content or affiliate
    recommendations. If either is introduced, the commercial relationship will be
    disclosed prominently on the affected page before the first compensated link
    or claim. Sponsored material will not be presented as independent editorial
    review. Affiliate compensation will not justify unsupported rankings or claims.
  </p>

  <h2>Reporting a problem</h2>
  <p>
    If a future ad is misleading, unsafe, inappropriately placed, or difficult to
    distinguish from site content, report the page and approximate time through
    the <a href="/contact/">contact page</a>. Do not click a suspicious ad merely
    to collect more information.
  </p>

  <RelatedReading links={[
    { href: '/editorial-policy/', label: 'Editorial independence', description: 'How commercial interests are kept out of editorial decisions.' },
    { href: '/privacy/', label: 'Privacy policy', description: 'Read current information about analytics, storage, and third parties.' },
    { href: '/corrections-policy/', label: 'Report a material issue', description: 'How factual and product problems are investigated.' },
  ]} />
</PageLayout>
